  "caption": "Quinn's first pickleball game was going brilliantly until a sudden thwack in the calf. Quinn turned around to find the culprit. Nobody was there.\n\nA sudden 'kick' feeling on push-off is often a calf strain, while a cramp tends to ease within minutes. A snap at the back of the ankle with weak push-off needs same-day assessment.\n\nWhat often helps: gentle movement, elevation and ice for comfort early, no hard stretching or deep massage at first, then calf raises progressed from two legs to one. Aim for about 20–25 single-leg raises and comfortable hopping before sport.\n\nCalf pain without an injury, especially with swelling, warmth or redness, needs prompt medical review. With chest pain or breathlessness, call 000.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
